---
import Page from "../layouts/Page.astro";
import { BUSINESS, LAST_UPDATED } from "../lib/site";
---

<Page
  title="Privacy notice | Waymark"
  description="How Waymark handles your information. Your study progress stays on your device, there is no account and no advertising tracking."
  heading="Privacy notice"
  lead="Short version: your study progress stays on your device. We don't need an account, we don't track you for advertising, and we never ask about your nationality or immigration status."
  updated={LAST_UPDATED}
>
  <h2>Who is responsible for your data</h2>
  <p>
    {BUSINESS.legalName} is the data controller. Contact: <a href={`mailto:${BUSINESS.privacy}`}>{BUSINESS.privacy}</a>.
    {BUSINESS.icoNumber ? <>ICO registration number: {BUSINESS.icoNumber}.</> : null}
  </p>

  <h2>What we collect and why</h2>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>Information</th><th>Why</th><th>Where it is kept</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td>Your study progress, test date and settings</td>
        <td>To run your study plan</td>
        <td>On your own device only. We cannot see it.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Emails you send us, including question reports</td>
        <td>To reply and fix problems</td>
        <td>Our email provider. Kept for up to 2 years.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Purchase details (name, email, payment), once payments open</td>
        <td>To take payment, give you access and meet tax and accounting rules</td>
        <td>Our payment provider and purchase-management provider. Kept for 6 years for accounting.</td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p>We do not collect your nationality, immigration status or any official ID.</p>

  <h2>Our legal reasons</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Running the study tool you asked for, and selling you access: <strong>contract</strong>.</li>
    <li>Keeping accounting records: <strong>legal obligation</strong>.</li>
    <li>Replying to emails and improving question accuracy: <strong>legitimate interests</strong>.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Who we share it with</h2>
  <p>
    Only the providers that help us run Waymark: website hosting (Vercel), email (Hostinger) and, once payments open,
    our payment provider (Stripe) and purchase-management provider (RevenueCat). Some of these process data outside
    the UK under safeguards approved by UK law. We never sell your data.
  </p>

  <h2>Cookies and tracking</h2>
  <p>We don't use advertising or tracking cookies. See our <a href="/cookies">cookie notice</a>.</p>

  <h2>Your rights</h2>
  <p>
    You can ask to see, correct or delete the information we hold about you, object to how we use it, or ask us to
    limit it. Your study progress is only on your device: you can delete it at any time in the app under Settings, then
    "Reset all progress".
  </p>

  <h2>Complaints</h2>
  <p>
    If you're unhappy with how we've handled your data, email <a href={`mailto:${BUSINESS.privacy}`}>{BUSINESS.privacy}</a>.
    We will acknowledge your complaint within 30 days and respond as quickly as we can. You can also complain to the
    Information Commissioner's Office at <a href="https://ico.org.uk/make-a-complaint/" rel="noopener">ico.org.uk</a>.
  </p>
</Page>
